'''Turoth''' are [[Slayer monsters]] that require a [[Slayer]] level of 55 to kill. They are melee based, and as such [[Protect from Melee]] will negate all of their damage. They drop [[herbs]] and [[seeds]] commonly, though not as frequently as [[aberrant spectre]]s, as well as frequent [[nature rune]]s. In addition, they also drop the [[leaf-bladed sword]] and [[necklace of fangs]].

Turoth, like [[kurask]], can only be damaged with [[leaf-bladed weapons]], [[broad arrows]] and [[broad bolts|bolts]], or the [[Magic Dart]] spell due to their thick hides.{{CiteNPC|npc=Slayer Master|quote=Turoth are large vicious creatures with thick hides. You'll need a Leaf-Tipped Spear, Sword or Battle-axe, Broad Arrows, or a Magic Dart to harm them.|loc=|notes=|name=}} Turoth are immune to other types of attacks, thereby establishing hidden skill requirements to kill them (particularly for [[ironmen]]). This also means the [[Dwarf Multicannon|dwarf multicannon]] is ineffective, and cannot be placed in this area. Though most of the means available for attacking them cannot inflict poison, it is still possible to inflict [[venom]] by using either a [[serpentine helm]] or a [[toxic staff of the dead]] with [[Magic dart|Magic Dart]].

Although turoth are invulnerable to any damage from the [[eldritch Nightmare staff]], [[Saradomin godsword]], and [[toxic blowpipe]] special attacks, they will still heal the player as if it would have dealt damage, making them useful as special attack weapons during extended trips. The [[ancient mace]] special attack also restores [[Prayer point]]s equal to the damage that would have been dealt. [[Guthan the Infested's equipment|Guthan's equipment's]] set effect does '''not''' work.

The majority of the Turoth in the [[Fremennik Slayer Dungeon]] are level 83 and 85, along with three level 87s, and one level 89.

